# Backend Sharp and Node

## Problem

`@strapi/plugin-upload` depends on **Sharp** for image processing. Older **Sharp 0.32.x** expects a legacy native layout (`build/Release/sharp-win32-x64.node`) and does not reliably install for **Node 22+**, which breaks `pnpm type:generate`, `strapi develop`, and any command that loads plugins.

## Fix in this repo

- Root [`package.json`](package.json) sets **`pnpm.overrides.sharp`** to **`0.34.5`** so every consumer (including Strapi) resolves the same Sharp. Sharp 0.34.x supports `^18.17.0 || ^20.3.0 || >=21.0.0` and uses **`@img/sharp-win32-x64`** (and siblings) for prebuilt binaries.
- [`apps/backend/package.json`](apps/backend/package.json) declares **`sharp`** explicitly at **`0.34.5`** (aligned with the override).

`pnpm` also lists **`sharp`** under **`onlyBuiltDependencies`** so install scripts run and native binaries are fetched.

## Strapi engine warning

Strapi 4.x still declares **`engines.node: <=20.x.x`**. You may see a pnpm **Unsupported engine** warning on Node 22; types and Sharp can work, but **Node 20 LTS** remains the safest choice for production and CI until Strapi officially supports newer Node.

## After changing Sharp or Node

From the monorepo root: `pnpm install`, then `pnpm --filter @repo/backend type:generate` (or `cd apps/backend && pnpm type:generate`).
